{
  "duration": 70.539,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.119,
      "end": 0.299,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.919,
      "end": 1.679,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.22,
      "end": 3.819,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.199,
      "end": 7.079,
      "text": "Now in this problem, a cube has an edge length of"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.679,
      "end": 8.579,
      "text": "four centimeter,"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.039,
      "end": 10.479,
      "text": "and we need to find its volume."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.019,
      "end": 11.619,
      "text": "What does"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.039,
      "end": 13.399,
      "text": "volume actually mean?"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.0,
      "end": 17.399,
      "text": "Imagine you have a small gift box shaped like a cube."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.879,
      "end": 18.92,
      "text": "The volume tells us"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.359,
      "end": 21.6,
      "text": "how much space is available inside that box."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.079,
      "end": 22.719,
      "text": "In other words,"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.319,
      "end": 24.319,
      "text": "how much it can hold."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.0,
      "end": 26.799,
      "text": "Here we are sure about one fact."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.34,
      "end": 27.879,
      "text": "In a cube,"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.579,
      "end": 30.359,
      "text": "all the edges are exactly the same."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.939,
      "end": 32.819,
      "text": "So if one edge is four centimeter,"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.399,
      "end": 34.419,
      "text": "the length is four,"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.939,
      "end": 36.219,
      "text": "the breadth is four,"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.619,
      "end": 38.299,
      "text": "and the height is also four."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.86,
      "end": 40.899,
      "text": "This is why the formula becomes very simple."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.459,
      "end": 48.619,
      "text": "Volume equal to side times side times side, or you can remember it as volume equal to side cube."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.0,
      "end": 50.079,
      "text": "Now let us put the value."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.639,
      "end": 53.18,
      "text": "Volume equal to four times four times four."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.619,
      "end": 58.919,
      "text": "First, four times four becomes 16, then 16 times four becomes 64."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.539,
      "end": 61.739,
      "text": "This means the cube can hold"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.18,
      "end": 64.819,
      "text": "64 cubic centimeter of space."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.659,
      "end": 70.539,
      "text": "So the final answer will be 64 cubic centimeter, which is option C."
    }
  ],
